\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Epistemic uncertainty ($\sigma $) distributions for benign and ransomware samples across all three agents. The Semantic Agent is near-deterministic ($\bar  {\sigma }\approx 0$); the Behavioural Agent shows low but non-trivial uncertainty ($\bar  {\sigma }\approx 0.013$); the Knowledge Agent exhibits the highest uncertainty ($\bar  {\sigma }\approx 0.055$), consistent with its smaller training set and heuristic label construction.\relax }}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
